        </div>

        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">No slip under your foot, two to three inches
            of lift at the centre of the deck.</strong> Both conditions, every
            time. Lubricate before you tighten, turn both rear bolts a quarter turn
            at a time, and re-check the lift after each one.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
            If the belt will not satisfy both conditions at once, it is stretched
            or the deck is dry — start with
            <a href="/how-often-to-lubricate-treadmill/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">the lubrication check</a>.
            Once tension is right, centre the belt using
            <a href="/how-to-center-treadmill-belt/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">the tracking guide</a>.
          </p>
        </div>
